# External dependencies of the RGA Workbench, one per line, each with what it is for.
# Anything compiled or fetched from source rather than linked carries its fetch command.

libglfw3-dev        # Windowing, input and GL context for the desktop build (apt).
libgl1-mesa-dev     # OpenGL headers and loader for the desktop build (apt).
libosmesa6-dev      # Software rasteriser, so headless capture runs with no GPU (apt).
zlib1g-dev          # Deflate streams for PNG export (apt).
xvfb                # Virtual X server, so the desktop build runs headless in CI (apt).
fontconfig          # Not linked: both targets ship their own faces, vendored below. Listed so a
                    #   reader knows the absence of a system font dependency is deliberate.

# Fetched, not linked. `tools/fetch_vendor.sh` runs both of these into `vendor/`.
pga                 # The rigid/conformal PGA library this workbench is a testbed for.
                    #   git clone https://gitlab.com/mraxilus/replications.git
                    #   commit f8861e0b5ab6e868382126aa7b109503f2fe16d3
                    #   path lengyel/projective_geometric_algebra_illuminated
                    #   licence Prosperity Public License 3.0.0 (noncommercial; see
                    #   vendor/pga/LICENSE.md, copied by the fetch script). Never committed.
stb_truetype.h      # Glyph rasterisation for the desktop font atlas; the GUI is hand-rolled,
                    #   so nothing else turns a TTF outline into coverage.
                    #   curl -L https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nothings/stb/master/stb_truetype.h
                    #   licence MIT / public domain (dual). Never committed.
fonts               # Every face both targets draw with, from the fontsource CDN at 5.3.0:
                    #   Noto Sans 400 and 600 (UI text), Noto Sans Math (operators, bold
                    #   operands), Noto Sans Symbols 2 (dual stars, abandon cross), Noto Serif
                    #   (prose), Commit Mono (code, data, figures). All SIL Open Font License
                    #   1.1; the licence text is fetched beside the files and kept with them.
                    #   base=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@fontsource
                    #   curl -LO $base/commit-mono/files/commit-mono-latin-400-normal.woff2
                    #   ... and the five Noto faces; `tools/fetch_vendor.sh` fetches all six
                    #   and converts each to TrueType for the desktop rasteriser. Never
                    #   committed.
fonttools, brotli   # Convert WOFF2 to TrueType for the desktop atlas, and subset each face to
                    #   the codepoints the tool writes for the browser page (pip).
